    {
      "@id": "device:pressureregulator001",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:Valve",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Pressure regulator 001",
      "rdfs:comment": "Pressure regulator in the hydrogen supply line: it holds the vessel at the set pressure by feeding gas on demand. A cpo:Valve (Laura Fadler, 15.10.2026; entered before the ontology had the class, as a plain cpo:Device). Modelled as an instrument, not as a segment of the flow path: it is not given ports or a contained material, because that would mean splitting the hydrogen stream.",
