    {
      "@id": "device:vial_template",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:Vessel",
        "hlo:Fixed",
        "hlo:Template"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Sample vial (template)",
      "rdfs:comment": "TEMPLATE, not a single identifiable object - see cpo:isSingleUse. A 2 mL screw-neck vial of the kind a GC autosampler takes; every sample drawn in every experiment goes into a fresh one, so the specializations of this entry are different pieces of glass rather than one vial used repeatedly. That is also why it carries no usage, calibration or service history: there is nothing whose history could be carried forward. Its screw cap and septum are devices of their own (device:vial_cap_template, device:vial_septum_template, since 2026-09-26): a cap is taken off and put back, so it is not a second phase of the vial body.",
      "cpo:isSingleUse": true,
      "cpo:isCompositeDevice": false,
      "cpo:canReceivePower": false,
      "cpo:hasPort": {
        "@id": "port:vial_template_opening"
      },
      "cpo:hasManufacturer": {
        "@id": "organization:ExampleCorp"
      },
      "cpo:locatedInsideOf": {
        "@id": "lab:L109"
      },
      "cpo:madeOfMaterial": {
        "@id": "material:vial_template_Body"
      },
      "cpo:definesForm": {
        "@id": "device:vial_template_Form"
      },
      "cpo:hasEnvelopeForm": {
        "@id": "device:vial_template_Form"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "port:vial_template_opening",
      "@type": [
        "cpo:DeviceOpening",
        "hlo:Fixed"
      ],
      "cpo:isPortOf": {
        "@id": "device:vial_template"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "device:syringe_template",
      "@type": [
        "sosa:Sampler",
        "hlo:Fixed",
        "hlo:Template"
      ],
      "schema:name": "Sampling syringe (template)",
      "rdfs:comment": "TEMPLATE, not a single identifiable object - see cpo:isSingleUse. A 1 mL disposable syringe, used once to draw a sample and then discarded; the specializations of this entry are different syringes, not one syringe used repeatedly, which is why it carries no usage, calibration or service history. Typed sosa:Sampler (a subclass of cpo:Device) the same way the instruments are typed sosa:Sensor - SOSA's own examples for a Sampler include a hypodermic syringe and needle. Since 27.09.2026 its barrel is a form with a cavity (device:syringe_template_Barrel) and the tip of its barrel a port (port:syringe_template_tip): the sample is a material of its own in the barrel between being drawn from the vessel and pushed into the vial. The needle is not modelled at all, not even as a body of its own: a steel needle beside the polypropylene barrel would be a second phase of the body material (a layer, rule 3.8a) without explaining anything here.",
      "cpo:isSingleUse": true,
      "cpo:isCompositeDevice": false,
      "cpo:canReceivePower": false,
      "cpo:hasManufacturer": {
