      "schema:name": "Capillary T2 of the K1 Start reactor, contact zone",
      "rdfs:comment": "Section of capillary T2: liquid 1 as a film on the wall with the air core in the middle - no reaction. From the end of T1 to the end of T2: the air leaving T1 meets liquid 1 and forces it into a thin film (the patent's liquid film forming section). Its length is assumed: the patent gives none, only that T2 ends downstream of T1 or with it - taken as 10 mm, twenty times the inner diameter of T2. Its cavity is the full bore of T2. Dimensions and material from the patent the K1 is built on - assumed, the commercial K1 may differ.",
      "schema:comment": "Added by curation; not in the ELN (Accelerated Materials, K1 Technical Data Sheet V20260220; Patent US11724241B2, 'Constant shear continuous reactor device' (N. Jose, A. Lapkin; Cambridge Enterprise), example annular microreactor; patents.google.com/patent/US11724241B2) - suggested by Claude Code, confirmed by Laura Fadler on 06.10.2026 for the series pba_synthesis.",
